cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite the cloth-fit tree it is vendored from and the paper it implements.
title: cloth-fit, intersection-free garment retargeting on PolyFEM (vendored)
abstract: >-
  V-Sekai-fire/cloth-fit at d2bd59a6 (tip of its default branch main/main),
  added here as a squashed git subtree: the reference implementation of
  Zizhou Huang's SIGGRAPH 2025 paper "Intersection-free Garment Retargeting"
  (https://huangzizhou.github.io/assets/img/research/cloth/paper.pdf), built
  on PolyFEM's nonlinear optimizers, linear solvers and IPC collision
  handling, with the org's commits on top that isolate the garment domain
  from base PolyFEM (POLYFEM_WITH_GARMENT), extract run_retarget, start the
  retarget from a feasible body and link PolyFEM_bin -static under
  llvm-mingw. It is the source of fit.elf (Cut 6) and of the native oracle
  in tools/native, which was built from this same tree: foxgirl_skirt, 1
  thread, 248 Newton iterations to step_garment_252.obj, bitwise
  reproducible. garment-data/ carries the four example avatars and
  garments (FoxGirl, Goblin, T-rex; skirt, jacket, jumpsuit) used as gate
  inputs. CPM pins as vendored: polysolve Huangzizhou#ee553dc6, ipc-toolkit
  Huangzizhou#993e7e0f, openvdb Huangzizhou#c96cb069, libigl v2.5.0,
  nlohmann_json v3.11.2 (via polysolve), oneTBB v2021.9.0; the native
  build takes the first five from the V-Sekai-fire forks in
  tools/forks.tsv through CPM_<pkg>_SOURCE (tools/forks/fetch.sh) without
  editing the recipes.
  OpenVDB replaced for fit.elf (Cut 6): (1) CMakeLists.txt no longer
  includes the openvdb recipe or links openvdb (cmake/recipes/openvdb.cmake
  stays, unused); the upstream oracle builds from the squash commit
  812ceb26 (tools/native/build_upstream.sh), not from this tree. (2) New
  src/polyfem/solver/forms/garment_forms/SdfGrid.{hpp,cpp}: the avatar SDF
  FitForm built with meshToSignedDistanceField(xform, Vec3s points, tris,
  {}, 150, 1), as a lazily filled brick grid; voxel (i,j,k) at world
  (i,j,k)*h, value clamp(sd, -h, 150h), sd the exact igl::AABB distance to
  the float-rounded avatar signed by igl::fast_winding_number (inside if
  w > 0.5); 8^3 bricks in an unordered_map, filled whole on first touch,
  each value a pure function of the voxel index; SdfGrid::cached() shares
  one grid per (avatar hash, voxel size) across the FitForm rebuilt every
  substep. (3) New garment_forms/SdfSpline.{hpp,cpp}: the call site of the
  Lean-emitted tricubic B-spline kernel (lean/Fit/SdfSplineHessian.lean ->
  kernels/fit/cpp/sdf_spline_hessian_emit.cpp) that replaces the openvdb
  fork's SplineSampler::sampleHessian; the CMake option FIT_KERNELS_PENDING
  (default ON; FIT_KERNELS_DIR and FIT_SLANG_PRELUDE_DIR when OFF) keeps
  the emit out until it lands, and the sampler throws meanwhile; no
  hand-written sampler is linked. (4) FitForm.{hpp,cpp}: the openvdb grid,
  accessor and HessType give way to SdfGrid and SdfHess; solution_changed
  gathers stencils and calls the kernel in batches of 1024 samples, then
  scales g/h and h/h^2 as before; the debug writes (fit-faces-debug.obj,
  and sdf.obj from volumeToMesh) are gone and out_dir, now unused,
  defaults to ""; the Hessian reserves fit_faces_ids.size()*81 triplets
  instead of 1e7; SDFCollisionForm (unused) is deleted. (5)
  tests/test_garment.cpp drops its SDFCollisionForm case and defines
  _USE_MATH_DEFINES for the M_PI the OpenVDB headers used to bring in.
  Checked by Gate 6a (gates/6-fit/sdf) against OpenVDB on the foxgirl
  oracle.
  The other fit.elf patches (POLYFEM_THREADING=NONE, embedded specs, no
  file I/O) will be listed here as they land.
type: software
authors:
